     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Anand Pandit Funds 1,000 Scholarships for Amitabh Bachchan's 84th Birthday</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Amitabh Bachchan</span> <span>#Anand Pandit</span></div>
       <p>Producer Anand Pandit has announced a significant educational initiative to commemorate Amitabh Bachchan's 84th birthday on October 11. In collaboration with the Lotus Foundation, Pandit will provide scholarships to 1,000 deserving students. This effort aims to honor the legendary actor through educational support for young people, as reported by Bollywood Hungama. The initiative celebrates Bachchan’s enduring legacy, emphasizing the values of perseverance, dedication, and excellence that have defined his career.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/anand-pandit-funds-1000-scholarships-for-amitabh-bachchans-8.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The celebrations for Bachchan's 84th birthday extend beyond the scholarship program. Hoardings are planned across Mumbai, and birthday greetings will be displayed on cinema screens throughout India, ensuring a widespread tribute to the veteran star. This comprehensive approach underscores the producer's admiration for Bachchan and his impact.</p><p>Pandit expressed his profound admiration for Bachchan, stating, “Every year, I find it difficult to put into words what Amit Ji means to me, both personally and as someone whose life has been shaped by cinema.” He highlighted Bachchan's consistent spirit, noting, &quot;What has always inspired me is not just the body of work he has created, but the spirit with which he continues to approach his craft. The fire we first witnessed in ‘Zanjeer’ is still burning bright.&quot; Pandit added that even today, Bachchan &quot;brings the energy of a newcomer to his work, along with the wisdom and gravitas of a master.”</p><p>For Pandit, the scholarship initiative serves as a means to extend this inspiration beyond the film industry to the next generation. He explained the thought behind the gesture, saying, “Amit Ji has shown us what dedication, resilience and the willingness to keep reinventing oneself can achieve. Through this initiative, I hope to celebrate not only the legend he is, but also the values he represents. If his journey can inspire young people to pursue their dreams with conviction, that is a legacy worth celebrating.”</p><p>This is not the first time Pandit has marked Bachchan’s birthday with initiatives focused on social contribution. On the actor’s 80th birthday in 2022, Pandit pledged meals for 8,000 children and donated 800 hearing aids. The following year, he dedicated more than 8,100 trees to Bachchan, establishing the ‘Amitabh Bachchan Grove’. With the current scholarship programme, Pandit once again commemorates Bachchan's birthday by placing education and social welfare at the core of the celebrations.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on scholarship application process and eligibility.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent work incorporating all available details, including historical context, direct quotes, and specific donor initiatives.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/anand-pandit-to-offer-scholarships-to-1000-students-as-part-of-celebrating-the-84th-birthday-of-amitabh-bachchan/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
