     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ashok Gehlot Accuses BJP of Discrediting Opposition Over Election Commission</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Former Rajasthan Chief Minister Ashok Gehlot accused the BJP of attempting to discredit the opposition for questioning the Election Commission regarding the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls. Gehlot alleged that BJP national president Nitin Nabin is acting as a legal representative for the Commission rather than addressing concerns about vote deletions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/ashok-gehlot-accuses-bjp-of-discrediting-opposition-over-ele.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Gehlot also condemned Nabin’s rhetoric regarding protesters, labeling the threats against those exercising democratic rights as inappropriate. The Congress leader claimed that the BJP, RSS, and the Election Commission collaborated on the electoral roll revision, while alleging that Nabin’s aggressive stance reflects direct instructions from Union Home Minister Amit Shah.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately captures Gehlot's accusations against the BJP and Nabin, reflecting the content of the provided report.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/bjp-discrediting-opposition-for-raising-questions-over-election-commission-ashok-gehlot/article71569089.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
