     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-10-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Christa Pike Discharged From Hospital Following Botched Execution</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Convicted murderer Christa Pike has been discharged from the hospital and returned to prison after surviving two lethal injections on September 30. The 50-year-old inmate, who spent 30 years on death row, regained consciousness and began speaking earlier this week, surprising medical staff and her legal team.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/christa-pike-discharged-from-hospital-following-botched-exec.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Tennessee officials have not yet indicated if they intend to reschedule the execution. A judge has ordered the state to preserve all evidence related to the failed attempt, which could serve as the basis for future litigation. Pike remains under medical care within the prison system following the unprecedented survival of a lethal injection procedure.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the key developments regarding Christa Pike's release and the legal implications of the failed execution.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
