       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Experts Call for More Humane IIT System</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#IIT</span> <span>#Higher Education</span> <span>#Inclusion</span> <span>#Student Pressure</span></div>
       <p>Education experts have urged a shift toward a more humane IIT system, arguing that current pressures compromise student well‑being. The commentary highlights that intense competition and rank‑centric culture create a stressful environment for aspirants. It also points to inclusion gaps, noting that many qualified candidates from marginalized backgrounds struggle to access the institutes. Together, the experts call for reforms that balance academic excellence with mental health support and broader equity measures.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/experts-call-for-more-humane-iit-system.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: policy proposals on IIT admission reforms.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is concise and accurately summarizes the provided source material regarding the call for a more humane IIT system.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
