       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Henderson and Caicedo Lead Chelsea to 5-1 Victory Over Bournemouth</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Chelsea secured a dominant 5-1 victory against Bournemouth on Saturday as manager Xabi Alonso deployed Jordan Henderson and Moises Caicedo in midfield for the first time. The duo provided critical stability for the side, which has struggled defensively this season despite scoring 15 goals in six matches. Henderson, signed on a free transfer from Brentford, scored two goals and provided an assist, becoming the third-oldest player to achieve the feat for the club.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/henderson-and-caicedo-lead-chelsea-to-5-1-victory-over-bourn.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Caicedo played 72 minutes in a deep-lying role, further anchoring the team's structure. Alonso praised the performance as the most complete of the season, highlighting the team's improved control and defensive balance.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the match performance, player contributions, and tactical context from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
