     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Home loan rates start at 7% across 12 public sector banks in October 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Home Loans</span> <span>#Interest Rates</span> <span>#Public Sector Banks</span></div>
       <p>Home loan rates begin at 7% at select public sector banks in October 2026, with major lenders such as State Bank of India, Bank of Baroda and Punjab National Bank offering the headline figure. The source advises borrowers to compare rates, loan slabs, fees and other borrowing costs before applying.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/home-loan-rates-start-at-7-across-12-public-sector-banks-in-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Rates differ by loan amount. Bank of Maharashtra and Central Bank of India start at 7% across all three slabs – up to ₹30 lakh, ₹30‑75 lakh and above ₹75 lakh – with overall ranges of 7‑9.90% and 7‑9.15% respectively. Other banks present varied bands, and the final rate depends on the lending institution, borrower profile, credit score, past borrowing history, loan amount and other factors.</p><p>For example, Canara Bank’s rates start at 7.25% for loans up to ₹30 lakh, 7.20% for ₹30‑75 lakh and 7.15% for amounts above ₹75 lakh. Punjab National Bank follows the same pattern, falling from 7.25% in the lowest slab to 7.20% in the higher slabs. Concessions are offered: Canara Bank adds a 5‑basis‑point discount for takeover or ready‑to‑move home loans and for salaried customers with a salary account; UCO Bank gives women borrowers a 0.05% cut and a 0.10% cut for takeover loans; Union Bank of India provides a 0.05% concession for borrowers who opt for an insurance policy.</p><p>Borrowers should evaluate the full cost of a home loan, not just the headline rate. Processing fees, tenure, overall interest costs, flexibility and penalties for missed repayments all affect the total outlay. Even a small rate difference can change the total interest payable over the loan’s life. The source, dated 7 October 2026, recommends verifying the latest rates with lenders and seeking advice from a certified financial advisor to secure the most suitable loan.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft provides a clear and accurate summary of the home loan rate landscape and the factors affecting borrowing costs.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/personal-finance/home-loan-rates-october-2026-compare-rates-starting-from-7-across-12-public-sector-banks-11791486253416.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
