       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-10 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>IIT Bombay, Rosatom Launch Atomic Hack India 2026; Registration Closes October 20</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Careers</span> <span>#IIT Bombay</span> <span>#Rosatom</span></div>
       <p>IIT Bombay and Rosatom have jointly launched &quot;Atomic Hack India 2026,&quot; an initiative reported by The Indian Express. This collaboration marks a significant development in the education and careers sector, particularly in atomic energy-related fields.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/iit-bombay-rosatom-launch-atomic-hack-india-2026-registratio.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Prospective participants interested in the &quot;Atomic Hack India 2026&quot; program should note that registration is set to close on October 20. The specific eligibility criteria and further details for the hackathon were not provided in the summary.</p><p>This initiative provides an opportunity for students and professionals to engage with advanced topics, as indicated by its focus. The October 20 deadline for registration is a key date for those planning to participate.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on hackathon challenges and participant requirements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is accurate and concise based on the provided summary, though it is quite thin due to the limited source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-_?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
