     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · Good News Network · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>KLM Pilot Zoë Flies Commercial Jet with Father as Captain, Mother as Cabin Crew</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Positive News</span> <span>#Aviation</span> <span>#Family</span> <span>#KLM</span></div>
       <p>A young pilot, 22-year-old Zoë, recently flew a commercial jet as co-pilot alongside her father, Michel, who served as captain, while her mother, Marjan, worked as a cabin crew member on the same flight. This marked the first time all three family members were on the same Dutch airline KLM flight, departing from Amsterdam. The unique alignment of their work schedules came as a complete surprise in August, as none of them initially realized their duties would place them together on this particular journey.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/klm-pilot-zoe-flies-commercial-jet-with-father-as-captain-mo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Zoë grew up watching her father head off to work in his pilot’s uniform, jetting off to far-flung destinations around the world. She recalled, “I remember my dad’s job seemed so mysterious, because I would never know where he was flying to. Then as I got older and visited him at work, I fell in love with it.” This experience profoundly inspired her own love of aviation, and she described it as &quot;amazing&quot; to finally share the experience of flying with both her parents. The occasion held a special significance for the family, as Zoë noted it &quot;felt like a full circle moment&quot; given that her parents, Michel and Marjan, had originally met while working on a flight themselves. Michel has been a pilot for 35 years, having completed his training in 1992.</p><p>Fascinated by her father's career from an early age, Zoë excelled in math and science at school before deciding to follow in his footsteps and pursue a life in the cockpit. She attended the KLM Flight Academy after being accepted at just 17 years old, graduating after two years of rigorous training. Since then, Zoë has been fortunate enough to fly with her father five times, and has also had one prior flight with her mother as part of the cabin crew.</p><p>Why it matters: This story highlights the inspiring power of family legacy and shared passion in career paths.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article captures all essential details from the source and provides a coherent narrative, including the background context of the parents' meeting.</p>
