     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Lyrical Evangelist Ezra Sastry Dies at 72</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Renowned lyrical evangelist and musician Ezra Sastry passed away from cardiac arrest at a Secunderabad hospital on Saturday at age 72. A prominent figure in the Telugu States for over five decades, Sastry was celebrated as a singer, songwriter, composer, and music therapist who dedicated his life to spreading Christian messages through music.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/lyrical-evangelist-ezra-sastry-dies-at-72.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>He is survived by his wife, daughter, and son. A funeral service is scheduled for Sunday, October 11, at 2 p.m. at the Centenary Baptist Church in Secunderabad, with burial to follow at the Secunderabad Christian Cemetery.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief provides a concise, accurate summary of the event and the funeral arrangements.</p>
