     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Business Standard · 2026-10-10 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Opposition Critiques Security Crackdown on CJP Protest</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Opposition leaders have condemned the heavy security measures and detention of protesters in Delhi following the Cockroach Janta Party's (CJP) call for a demonstration at Jantar Mantar. Congress leader Rahul Gandhi predicted the government's downfall, while the Aam Aadmi Party described the restrictions as a &quot;black emergency.&quot;</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/opposition-critiques-security-crackdown-on-cjp-protest.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The CJP protest aims to demand the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar over alleged voter-list manipulation. Despite police denying permission and detaining approximately 200 demonstrators, opposition figures have criticized the use of force and police surveillance, urging the government to engage with the concerns of young protesters rather than suppressing their right to assemble.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the political fallout and opposition reaction as reported in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/black-emergency-cjp-protest-rahul-gandhi-arvind-kejriwal-aap-congress-jantar-mantar-126101000261_1.html" rel="noopener">Business Standard</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
