     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-10 · editor 7/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Screen Addiction's Toll on Young Minds Explored on World Mental Health Day</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health</span> <span>#Mental Health</span> <span>#Screen Addiction</span> <span>#Youth</span></div>
       <p>On World Mental Health Day, ETHealthworld highlighted the pervasive nature of screen usage, noting that &quot;the scroll rarely stops&quot; — from daily commutes to dinner tables and even in the moments before sleep. The report explores the significant toll that screen addiction can take on young minds.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/screen-addictions-toll-on-young-minds-explored-on-world-ment.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The article delves into identifying the warning signs associated with excessive screen time and digital dependency among youth. It also aims to provide insights into &quot;small changes that help&quot; mitigate these negative impacts, as stated by ETHealthworld.</p><p>The continuous engagement with screens across various daily activities underscores a growing concern for mental well-being. World Mental Health Day serves as a timely reminder to address these issues and understand their implications for younger generations.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on warning signs and practical solutions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate summary of the source, though it remains quite brief due to the limited nature of the provided summary text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/world-mental-health-day-the-toll-of-endless-scrolling-on-young-minds/134849416" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-10/screen-addictions-toll-on-young-minds-explored-on-world-ment" data-title="Screen Addiction's Toll on Young Minds Explored on World Mental Health Day"><b>Share:</b>
