       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana Congress Leaders Summoned to Delhi for Anti-SIR Rally</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Telangana Pradesh Congress Committee has directed all party MPs, MLAs, MLCs, and senior district leaders to report to New Delhi by October 12. The directive, issued by TPCC president B. Mahesh Kumar Goud following instructions from AICC general secretary K.C. Venugopal, is being treated as a priority.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/telangana-congress-leaders-summoned-to-delhi-for-anti-sir-ra.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Party members are gathering in the capital to participate in a national rally demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. The protest specifically calls for the scrapping of the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls, with delegations from across India expected to join the demonstration.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the directive issued to Telangana Congress leaders and the purpose of the upcoming rally.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/telangana-congress-leaders-called-to-delhi-on-october-12/article71569013.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
