       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · Times of India · 2026-10-10 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Tennessee Death Row Inmate Christa Pike Returns to Prison After Failed Execution</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Christa Pike, a 50-year-old Tennessee death row inmate, has returned to the Debra K. Johnson Rehabilitation Center following a failed lethal injection attempt on September 30. Pike, convicted for the 1995 murder of classmate Colleen Slemmer, required hospitalization and a ventilator after the procedure was aborted.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/tennessee-death-row-inmate-christa-pike-returns-to-prison-af.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Governor Bill Lee has suspended all 2026 executions and ordered an independent investigation into the state's procedures. The incident, which also prompted the resignation of Correction Commissioner Frank Strada, remains under review as legal teams seek evidence regarding the failure of the intravenous lines.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately synthesizes the key events, including the inmate's return, the governor's actions, and the official's resignation.</p>
