       <h1>Two Tornadoes Strike Marsala, Sicily, Causing Dozens of Injuries</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tornadoes</span> <span>#Sicily</span> <span>#Extreme Weather</span></div>
       <p>The coastal town of Marsala in western Sicily has been severely impacted by two tornadoes that struck the area, resulting in dozens of injuries and significant damage to buildings. The powerful storm approached the Sicilian town from the Mediterranean, bringing with it destructive force.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-10/two-tornadoes-strike-marsala-sicily-causing-dozens-of-injuri.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Among the structures damaged was a school, and numerous cars were overturned by the intense winds. A series of videos began circulating on Friday morning, capturing the dramatic sight of two waterspouts as they advanced from the sea towards the town, prompting residents to brace for their impending arrival.</p><p>What to watch: Local authorities' assessment of the full extent of damage and recovery efforts in Marsala.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the provided text regarding the tornadoes in Sicily.</p>
